From: OpenDesk <opendesk@openharmony.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Mar 2026 13:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix distutils/util.py platform string for HarmonyOS

Problem:
- get_host_platform() returns "ohos-harmonyos-aarch64" (with osname included)
- But sysconfig.get_platform() returns "harmonyos-aarch64"
- This causes two different build directories and module import fails

Root cause:
- The patch added "ohos-%s-%s" % (osname, machine) which includes osname
- Should return just "ohos-%s" % (machine,) to be consistent

Solution:
- Return "ohos-aarch64" (without osname) to match sysconfig format

--- a/Lib/distutils/util.py
+++ b/Lib/distutils/util.py
@@ -92,7 +92,8 @@ def get_host_platform():
         osname, release, machine = _osx_support.get_platform_osx(
                                         distutils.sysconfig.get_config_vars(),
                                         osname, release, machine)
+    elif osname[:9] == "harmonyos":
+        return "ohos-%s" % (machine,)
 
     return "%s-%s-%s" % (osname, release, machine)
 
